# Register Bank Using Verilog

## Description
A 4-bit Register Bank containing four registers (R0, R1, R2, R3). It supports writing and reading data using a 2-bit address.

## Features
- Four 4-bit registers
- Write enable
- Asynchronous reset
- Clock-based writing
- Combinational reading

## Working Principle
- When reset is HIGH, all registers are cleared to `0000`.
- When enable is HIGH, data is written into the selected register on the rising edge of the clock.
- When enable is LOW, the stored data remains unchanged.
- The address selects which register's data appears at the output.

## Tools Used
- Verilog HDL
- EDA Playground
- Icarus Verilog
- EPWave

